return {h=17,w=766,cr=75,hc=20,bh=70,gr="medium",eg={"water1","ground"},st={80,82,78,95,80,85},ab={{6,0},{13,0},{33,1}},genus={en="Duck Pokémon",es="Pokémon Pato",pt="Pokémon Pato"},flavor={en={[1]="Often seen swimming elegantly by lake shores. It is often mistaken for the Japanese monster, Kappa.",[2]="Often seen swimming elegantly by lake shores. It is often mistaken for the Japanese monster, Kappa.",[3]="Its slim and long limbs end in broad flippers. They are used for swimming gracefully in lakes.",[4]="When it swims at full speed using its long, webbed limbs, its forehead somehow begins to glow.",[5]="It appears by waterways at dusk. It may use tele kinetic powers if its forehead glows mysteriously.",[6]="It swims gracefully along on the quiet, slow-moving rivers and lakes of which it is so fond.",[7]="The webbed flippers on its forelegs and hind legs and the streamlined body of GOLDUCK give it frightening speed. This Pokémon is definitely much faster than even the most athletic swimmer.",[8]="GOLDUCK is the fastest swimmer among all Pokémon. It swims effortlessly, even in a rough, stormy sea. It sometimes rescues people from wrecked ships floundering in high seas.",[9]="A GOLDUCK is an adept swimmer. It sometimes joins competitive swimmers in training. It uses psychic powers when its forehead shimmers with light.",[10]="The forelegs are webbed, helping to make it an adept swimmer. It can be seen swimming elegantly in lakes, etc.",[11]="Often seen swimming elegantly by lakeshores. It is often mistaken for the Japanese monster Kappa.",[12]="A Pokémon that lives in lakes. It swims faster than any human swimming champion.",[13]="The flippers of its well-developed limbs give it shocking speed. It is the best swimmer among Pokémon.",[14]="It is seen swimming dynamically and elegantly using its well-developed limbs and flippers.",[15]="When it swims at full speed using its long, webbed limbs, its forehead somehow begins to glow.",[16]="It appears by waterways at dusk. It may use telekinetic powers if its forehead glows mysteriously.",[17]="It is seen swimming dynamically and elegantly using its well-developed limbs and flippers.",[18]="It is seen swimming dynamically and elegantly using its well-developed limbs and flippers.",[21]="When its forehead shines mysteriously, Golduck can use the full extent of its power.",[22]="When its forehead shines mysteriously, Golduck can use the full extent of its power.",[23]="It appears by waterways at dusk. It may use telekinetic powers if its forehead glows mysteriously.",[24]="The forelegs are webbed, helping to make it an adept swimmer. It can be seen swimming elegantly in lakes, etc.",[25]="The webbed flippers on its forelegs and hind legs and the streamlined body of Golduck give it frightening speed. This Pokémon is definitely much faster than even the most athletic swimmer.",[26]="Golduck is the fastest swimmer among all Pokémon. It swims effortlessly, even in a rough, stormy sea. It sometimes rescues people from wrecked ships floundering in high seas.",[27]="It is said that the red part of its forehead grants supernatural powers to those who possess one, so it was over-hunted in the past.",[28]="It swims along the banks of lakes and catches fish Pokémon. It takes them to the shore and quietly eats them up.",[29]="Even fast-swimming fish Pokémon can be disabled by Golduck. It brings them to a standstill and seizes them.",[30]="A professional swimmer, it can continue swimming for two days straight by waving its long tail skillfully.",[31]="Its long, slim limbs end in broad flippers. They are used for swimming gracefully in lakes.",[32]="Its long, slim limbs end in broad flippers. They are used for swimming gracefully in lakes.",[33]="This Pokémon lives in gently flowing rivers. It paddles through the water with its long limbs, putting its graceful swimming skills on display.",[34]="Old tales tell of Golduck punishing those that defiled its river. The guilty were dragged into the water and taken away.",[39]="Its body is strong, and it has webbing on its hands and feet. Golduck can swim easily through rough seas, clawing its way through the high waves."},es={[23]="Aparece en ríos al anochecer. Puede usar poderes telequinéticos si su frente brilla misteriosamente.",[24]="Las patas traseras palmípedas le permiten nadar. Es común verlo chapotear con estilo en lagos y otras zonas acuáticas.",[25]="Golduck alcanza una velocidad de vértigo gracias a las aletas palmípedas de las extremidades y a la forma aerodinámica de su cuerpo. Realmente, la velocidad de este Pokémon supera la de cualquier nadador.",[26]="Golduck es el nadador más rápido de los Pokémon. Además, nada sin esfuerzo hasta en aguas turbulentas en plena tormenta. En ocasiones, ha rescatado a náufragos en alta mar.",[27]="En el pasado fue objeto de una caza indiscriminada, pues se decía que la parte roja de su frente daba poderes a quien la poseyera.",[28]="Se sumerge en las aguas de los lagos en busca de Pokémon pez para luego darse un apacible banquete en la orilla.",[29]="Puede paralizar incluso a los Pokémon pez más veloces, lo que le permite atraparlos con suma facilidad.",[30]="Un portento de la natación capaz de nadar durante dos días sin interrupción moviendo su larga cola con destreza.",[31]="Sus delgadas y largas extremidades terminan en dedos palmeados muy desarrollados que le permiten nadar en los lagos con gracilidad.",[32]="Sus delgadas y largas extremidades terminan en dedos palmeados muy desarrollados que le permiten nadar en los lagos con gracilidad.",[33]="Habita en ríos de aguas plácidas. Sus largas extremidades le permiten nadar con gracilidad.",[34]="Cuenta una antigua leyenda que los Golduck arrastraban a quienes contaminaran sus ríos al fondo de las aguas."},pt="Tem o corpo forte e membranas nas mãos e nos pés. Golduck nada com facilidade em mares agitados, abrindo caminho pelas ondas altas."},evo={{s=54},{s=55,from=54,c={{t="level-up",lv=33}}}},moves={[1]={1,10,1,39,1,5